rewrite_durably reads a failed stat of the file as an empty file, so it
rewrites nothing and syncs pages a failed fdatasync left clean and unwritten.
resume() and the open after a crash then build a hint over bytes the device
does not hold. The stat is std::filesystem::file_size's, which the counted
fault sweep reaches only because bytecask_tests links the C++ library
statically (#319).
Guarded-by: "fault sweep: resume after a failed sync"

